17592186336191 1089 "q-47485" 13194139535185 true] [17592186336191 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535185 true] [17592186336191 1100 "A baseball is hit by a batter. The distance between the batter and the ball, measured in miles, is given by the function $s(t)$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $0.015$ | $0.03$ | $0.045$ | $0.05$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity ${s}^{′}(t)$ when $t=1$ using a backward difference approximation." 13194139535185 true] [17592186336191 1113 #uuid "c4fbb16c-9818-55d9-b0fe-3dcb50b4a1b7" 13194139535185 true] [17592186336191 1145 "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{s(t)-s(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{s(1)-s(1-0.5)}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(1)-s(0.5)}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.03-0.015}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.015}{0.5} \\\\  & =0.03.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is $0.03\\,\\text{mi}/\\text{s}.$" 13194139535185 true] [17592186336192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336193 13194139535185 true] [17592186336192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336194 13194139535185 true] [17592186336192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336195 13194139535185 true] [17592186336192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336196 13194139535185 true] [17592186336192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336197 13194139535185 true] [17592186336192 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535185 true] [17592186336192 1041 "selection" 13194139535185 true] [17592186336192 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336197 13194139535185 true] [17592186336192 1110 #uuid "1b11ff88-8211-5080-ace3-99db4ef73418" 13194139535185 true] [17592186336193 1034 "0.02\\,\\text{mi}/\\text{s}" 13194139535185 true] [17592186336193 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535185 true] [17592186336193 1111 #uuid "05c6